  "RQ4 data_available": "yes https://github.com/isamuisozaki/AI-Pentest-Benchmark",
  "RQ5 risks_addressed": "Malicious actors training LLMs for real-world cyberattacks; sensitive-data access; forgetting, hallucinations, repeated commands, and human evaluation errors/bias",
  "RQ5 mitigations": "Responsible development and ethical oversight; strict human-action rules and attempt limits; summary memory, structured task management, and RAG",
  "author_limitations (verbatim)": "Due to time and cost constraints, we conducted ablations on only 2 boxes; further studies on additional machines could provide more comprehensive insights.",
  "author_future_work (verbatim)": "One area we are interested in pursuing is to increase the capability of our LLMs for Penetration Testing through Reinforcement Learning. We want to begin with a Penetration Testing Game with easier boxes, such as the boxes used in Happe, et al [Happe et al., 2024].",
